==Enemy==
Queen B rapidly fires moderately strong Area Attacks from extreme range that slow cats for 7.4 seconds on hit, and much like [[Cruel Angel Clionel]], her massive blind spot is often heavily covered by support, making most of her fights easier said than done.

==Strategy==
It is almost mandatory to acquire all [[anti-unstarred Alien Treasures]] from [[Into the Future]], or else you'll be facing off against a '''10 million HP''' monstrosity with an insane '''85,554''' damage. Her fast attack rate only makes this worse, and anything that ''does'' survive is slowed indefinitely, so make sure to get those Treasures! Fast cats such as [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]], [[Express Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Maglev Cat]], [[Crazed Cow Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Cow Cat]] and [[Swimmer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Butterfly Cat]] can easily get into her blind spot and capitalize from there. Unit Speed UP [[Cat Combo]]s help as well.

For cats that are not as fast as [[Crazed Cow Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Cow]], precise timing is required to get them past Queen B's attack hitbox; the specific bar is for units with over 12 speed, and if you cannot do that, luring her to the base is another option. [[:Category:Cats with Slow Immunity|Cats with slow immunity]] like [[Rover Cat (Rare Cat)|Catellite]] are also useful, since as long as they're slow-immune and can't be moved easily by her damage, Queen B alone won't be able to stop them. Based on calculations, any unit with at least 9 speed can enter her blind spot just in time. If you decide to sacrifice some of your [[Cat Base]] health and lure, you can time your units into Queen B's blind spot that usually wouldn't be able to enter it.

